RED FLAG 1 — TABLE PAGE OVERFLOW (HIGHEST PRIORITY, EI + RS)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bug: EI element tables (24-25 columns) and RS wide solvent tables run past the
page edge on every product — content clipped, looks broken. Seen on Vasopressin,
Carboprost, Esomeprazole, Chlorpromazine.
Fix (renderer, all doc types):
1. Element/solvent-matrix tables render in A4 LANDSCAPE section (page size swap
   for those tables only; narrative stays portrait).
2. Split EI element tables by class (Class1+2A / 2B / 3) — already partly done —
   AND cap each sub-table so total column count × min width ≤ landscape width.
   If a class still overflows, wrap to a second table continuation.
3. Auto-fit column widths; concentration/exposure cells to 4 significant figs
   max (0.15 not 0.1500; 1188.0 not 1188.000000). Trim trailing zeros.
4. Reduce table font (e.g. 7-8pt) for wide matrices; header bold.
5. Freeze first two label columns; never let a single table exceed the printable
   width. Verify no cell is clipped at the right margin.
Acceptance: no table crosses the page boundary in any EI or RS output; all
element/solvent columns fully visible in landscape.

RED FLAG 2 — INJECTION COLUMN HEADERS/VALUES WRONG (EI + RS)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bug: For injections the AI shows Column1="mg/dose"=36000 and Column2="Qty in
MDD (mg)"=36000 for Dextrose. Both wrong. Approved uses Column1="Qty/mL (mg)"=50
(per-mL quantity) and Column2="Amount in maximum dose (g)"=36.
Fix:
- Injection tables: Column1 = Qty per mL (mg/mL) — the composition per-mL value,
  NOT the amount in max dose. Dextrose=50, Acetic=0.0546, Na acetate=0.012.
- Column2 = Amount in maximum dose in GRAMS = qty_per_mL × daily_volume_mL / 1000.
  Dextrose = 50 × 720 / 1000 = 36 g.
- Solid OSD keeps mg/dose = qty_per_unit × doses; amount in mg.
- Daily Exposure = amount_in_max_dose_g × conc_µg_per_g (EI) — unchanged.
Acceptance (Vaso 20u): Dextrose Qty/mL=50, Amount=36 g; Acetic 0.0546/0.03931 g;
Na acetate 0.012/0.00864 g; Vasopressin 0.000377/0.000272 g.

RED FLAG 3 — BELOW-LIMIT / "<30% PERM CONC" → 0 (EI ONLY)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bug: Merck EMPROVE CoAs report every element "<30% of Option-1 permitted conc"
(qualitative below-limit). Approved uses ZERO. AI kept the 30%-of-Option-1 ppm
(0.45,0.06,0.15,0.6,7.5,21,33…) as real values → huge fake exposures → false
FAIL (Pb 3605% PDE). ND=0 convention (EI):
Fix (annexure_converter + EI):
- "<X" / "≤X" / "BDL" / "BLQ" / "Below LOD/LOQ" / "ND" / "Not detected" /
  "<30% of Perm Conc" / "meets/below Option 1" → concentration_value = 0.0.
  Keep observed_level raw text for audit. Only an explicit measured number with
  a real unit (ppm/ppb/µg/g) is a value.
- EXCEPTION (presence-flagged): a CoA with a "Likely Present = Yes" checkbox and
  a bound ABOVE the detection floor (e.g. Ni "<0.7", MRL 0.05, marked Yes) →
  keep the bound (0.7). To decide 0-vs-keep, read THREE fields: the <X value,
  the presence flag (if the format has one), and the MRL/Option-1 reference
  (X at the detection floor or =30%×Option-1 → 0; X above floor + Yes → keep).
- "Not intentionally added" declaration with no measured table → all 0.
- IGNORE CONEG/RoHS "Pb+Cd+Cr(VI)+Hg as a sum 100 ppm" packaging limits (West
  stopper) — never per-element EI values.
Acceptance (Vaso): all excipient "<30% Perm Conc" → 0; Table 4 excipient rows 0;
conclusion PASS, no confirmatory testing.

RED FLAG 4 — RS BELOW-LIMIT KEEPS NMT SPEC (RS ONLY — OPPOSITE OF EI)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bug risk: applying EI's ND=0 to RS would wrongly zero every solvent.
Rule (RS): a solvent batch result BDL/BLQ/ND that has an accompanying vendor NMT
SPECIFICATION limit → use the NMT spec as worst-case, NOT zero. Only zero a
solvent when there is NO spec AND it is declared NIL/absent.
Verified correct in Chlorpromazine run: Toluene BLQ(5.53)+NMT890→890;
t-Butanol BDL+NMT68→68; DMSO BDL+NMT5000→5000. KEEP this behavior; do not
regress by importing EI ND=0 into RS.

RED FLAG 5 — SALT/BASE FOOTNOTE IN INJECTION DOSING (EI + RS)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bug: Carboprost footnote "#332 mcg tromethamine ≡ 250 mcg carboprost" ignored;
volume derived off salt (332) not base (250).
Fix: parse composition footnote markers (#,*,@,superscript); classify salt/base
vs overage vs q.s. vs informational; for salt/base use BASE for daily-volume /
multiplier, SALT weight for component amounts. Chlorpromazine HCl and Vasopressin
are salt-basis MDD → NO conversion; their "#" markers are vendor/informational.
Warning-only if a marker has no footnote (never hard-block; default factor 1.0).

RED FLAG 6 — INGREDIENT COLUMN DETECTION (EI + RS)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bug: Chlorpromazine Excel with a "Pharmaceutical Function" column → parser used
"Antioxidant"/"Tonicity agent" as ingredient NAMES → nothing mapped → empty doc.
Carboprost/Vaso "Quantity per mL" / "Quantity/Vial" headers unrecognized.
Fix (RS + EI composition parser):
- Ingredient-name column: prefer headers "ingredient"/"material name"/"name of
  ingredient"/"component". EXPLICITLY EXCLUDE any header containing
  "function"/"role"/"category"/"purpose" from being the name column; read it as
  the ROLE field instead (for q.s./active detection).
- Quantity columns: recognize "quantity per ml", "quantity/vial", "qty/1ml",
  "qty/2ml", "quantity per 1ml/2ml", "mg/ml", plus existing hints.
- Injection mg-basis: daily_volume = MDD ÷ api_conc_per_mL (2400÷25=96;
  144units÷0.2=720). Do NOT compute implied_strength=MDD÷doses for mg/mL
  injections (that's for solid tablet strengths). Dedup identical-concentration
  columns (Qty/1mL & Qty/2mL both 25mg/mL → one).
- Self-test FAIL if ingredient names resolve to function words
  (antioxidant/tonicity/buffer/vehicle/active-as-a-name).

