RED FLAG 10 — CANONICAL SOLVENT ALIAS DEDUP (RS)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bug: DMSO appeared TWICE — "Dimethyl Sulphoxide" (API COA) and "Dimethyl
sulfoxide" (API decl) as two solvent columns → double-count.
Fix: normalize British/American spelling: sulphoxide=sulfoxide, sulphate=sulfate,
-ph-/-f-. Merge to ONE canonical DMSO. General: apply spelling normalization
before alias lookup so one solvent never appears twice.

RED FLAG 11 — DISPLAY-NAME GRADE STRIP + NO "–"/BLACK BOX (EI + RS)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Strip vendor grade (EMPROVE/EXPERT/ESSENTIAL/bio) INCLUDING ® and trailing
